# Variáveis de serviços
@auth = http://localhost:8081
@events = http://localhost:8083
@ticket = http://localhost:8086
@payment = http://localhost:8085

### 1) Criar usuário (Auth)
POST {{auth}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Teste Payment",
  "email": "teste.payment@example.com",
  "password": "minhasenha123"
}

# pega id do usuário
@userId = {{createUser.response.body.id}}

### 2) Login (obter token)
POST {{auth}}/auth/login/password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "teste.payment@example.com",
  "password": "minhasenha123"
}

# pega access token
@accessToken = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 3) Criar evento (Events)
POST {{events}}/api/events
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "name": "Show Teste",
  "date": "2025-12-01T20:00:00",
  "venue": "São Teste"
}

@eventId = {{createEvent.response.body.id}}

### 4) Criar assentos para o evento (Ticket Service)
POST {{ticket}}/api/seats?eventId={{eventId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

[
  "A1",
  "A2"
]

### 5) Criar reserva (Ticket Service)
POST {{ticket}}/api/reservations?userId={{userId}}&eventId={{eventId}}&ttlSeconds=300
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

[
  "A1",
  "A2"
]

@reservationId = {{create.response.body.id}}

### 6) Criar pagamento (Payment Service) — cenário SUCESSO
POST {{payment}}/api/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "reservationId": "{{reservationId}}",
  "userId": "{{userId}}",
  "amount": 150.00,
  "method": "CREDIT_CARD",
  "card": {
    "number": "4111111111111111",
    "expiry": "12/26",
    "cvv": "123"
  }
}

# Depois de sucesso, a reserva deve ser commitada pelo payment-service -> a reserva deixará de existir

### 7) Verificar reserva (deve retornar 404 se commitado)
GET {{ticket}}/api/reservations/{{reservationId}}
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 8) Simular falha: pagamento para reservation inexistente (deve retornar 502)
POST {{payment}}/api/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "reservationId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "userId": "{{userId}}",
  "amount": 150.00,
  "method": "CREDIT_CARD"
}

### Observações
# - Se quiser conferir o ticket gerado, use diretamente o endpoint de commit do ticket-service:
#   POST {{ticket}}/api/reservations/{{reservationId}}/commit
#   (isso retornará o TicketResponse — atenção: se o payment-service já tiver efetuado o commit a reserva não existirá)